            <div xml:id="d317">

                <pb facs="0539" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Norway/17: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-13T14:00:00+01:00">November 13,
                            1935—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 14—4:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Department’s telegram No. 16, November 12, 4 p.m. Note in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Anders</hi> case, which was sent the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs July 18, was followed October 17 by oral request for expedition of
                    reply, supplemented by memorandum same date. Oral representations and note
                    regarding <hi rendition="#italic">Anders, Trajan</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Reidun</hi> cases made at the Foreign Office today. It
                    has today been ascertained from appropriate official that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Anders</hi> case has been referred by the Ministry of
                    Commerce to the Minister of Justice; that judicial investigation is now being
                    made and that pertinent note will be sent very shortly to the Legation. Despatch
                        follows.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d317-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
